#010 | 2026-03-11
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/btw review different algorithms that are commonly used in video games and
replace floodfill and other algorithms that may not be as useful for the AI agent
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Response summary:
  - Removed FloodFillAgent (basic BFS frontier — redundant with A*)
  - Added ThetaStarAgent: any-angle pathfinding via Theta* algorithm
      * Bresenham line-of-sight check allows shortcuts across grid diagonals
      * Produces smoother paths through Doom's corridors; used in strategy
        game research (StarCraft II, top-down RPGs)
  - Added PotentialFieldsAgent: reactive artificial potential fields
      * No path planning — computes attractive force toward unexplored cells
        + repulsive forces from walls every frame
      * Smooth, real-time obstacle avoidance; used in robotics and as a
        local-avoidance layer in modern game engines
      * Stuck detection + random spin to escape local minima
  - Final AI agent roster: random, wander, heuristic, astar,
    theta_star, dijkstra, potential_fields

