#030 | 2026-03-18
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
make sure the player finds a path through each level without getting stuck into
a corner
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Response summary:
  - Root cause: BFS wandering fallback used direct _steer() toward unexplored
    cell, ignoring walls between agent and target — agent would drive into corners
  - Fix 1: All BFS wandering fallbacks now use A* (max_nodes=2000) to compute a
    wall-avoiding next step instead of steering straight at the target.
    Applied in _GridAgent.act() and both BFS fallbacks in FlowFieldAgent.act()
  - Fix 2: Stuck recovery (stuck_t >= 30) now also forces a replan/_field_t=0
    (picks a fresh target) and adds BTN_MOVE_BACKWARD + random turn to physically
    escape the corner, rather than just pressing USE in place
  - Changes confined to agent.py only

